{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/369","id":4719162790,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGUi1pg","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/369","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/369.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/369.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/369","number":369,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"2302055: reviewed scoped Liouville criteria, original unresolved (5/5)","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Accept scoped partial findings for Hayman–Lingham Problem 2.55 (2302055 / AMR-022-2055). The original question remains **unsolved, 5/5**: for three arbitrary nonconstant entire one-variable inputs, constancy of every ambient entire function bounded on the full separated-sum hypersurface is not established, and no admissible bounded nonconstant restriction is constructed.\n\nThe strongest explicit positive result allows one input R(exp(Q)), with R a nonconstant Laurent polynomial and Q a nonconstant polynomial, while the other two inputs are arbitrary nonconstant entire functions. The packet also proves the two-way polynomial-precomposition equivalence, a sufficient virtually nilpotent inverse-monodromy criterion under an explicit finite-exclusion surjective-cover hypothesis, and character/finite-dimensional-deck-orbit rigidity on the triple-double-exponential test. The non-ultra-Liouville quotient, wreath-product monodromy and infinite-dimensional representation examples are proof-route obstructions, not counterexamples to the original question.\n\nClassical dependencies remain credited: Demailly–Wakabayashi, Lin–Zaidenberg and Rubel–Squires–Taylor. The last theorem's applicable statement is checked in Demailly's primary publication; its complete original Annals proof was not retrieved. No novelty or current-open certification is inferred from historical bounded searches, and the historical branch/ref search counts were not independently reconstructed. The double-exponential test is unresolved in this attempt; no separate current-open claim is made for it.\n\nRoot source-first and mathematics-only reconstructions preceded implementation/results/status/final/history/review and substantive sibling access. Three independent families likewise sealed their mathematical verdicts first. A separately bound chronology clarification records that the function-theory family's supplementary Bishop/Picard full source confirmation came after its mathematical seal; this affects only the extra entire-curve source-access description and no candidate theorem. The original family seals remain unchanged.\n\nRoot reproduction validates all50 original Git/API files, all49 target artifacts, nine manifests/211 binding instances and five actual author checkpoints. All seven complete program outputs reproduce byte-for-byte: 38,066 author assertions and1,420 historical independent controls. Three new families add1,262 separately reproduced finite controls. These checks supplement the analytic proofs, without certifying a universal Liouville theorem by sampling. Fresh exact-head/body/base/tree and whole-package gates must pass before merge, and actual merge files/parents/queue are read back afterward.\n\nOpenAI tools were used extensively in research, proof drafting and adversarial verification. This is an unrefereed, AI-assisted partial research packet; no human peer review is claimed. Accept as partial work with the original problem unsolved. No paper, Zenodo upload, DOI, tracker row or release is associated with this acceptance. Only this problem's queue status/turn cells change against current main; all other queue bytes and original mathematical files are preserved.\n","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:00:25Z","updated_at":"2026-10-03T13:14:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"194b3acd4ff565dee9cf632c243b041c733ed1c3","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/369/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/369/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/369/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/f8c075b4018afb91b048e378e884382e8ba3f108","head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:math/2302055-reviewed-liouville-criteria","ref":"math/2302055-reviewed-liouville-criteria","sha":"f8c075b4018afb91b048e378e884382e8ba3f108","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url